      "path": "tooling/xtask/src/tasks/android_reference_membership.rs",
      "line": 1010,
      "title": "Accepted split filter shapes can still describe a producer-rejected aggregate",
      "finding": "The new split validation accepts any string/None test_filter, then publishes child relationships with aggregate_membership=true. A literal test_filter=\"(\" fails the pinned _validate_split_test_filter; two entries with absent, null or empty filters fail _gen_split_test_excludes because multiple catch-all splits are rejected. Current derivation records neither known rejection and emits an aggregate relationship despite that producer control flow. Generic unverified glob/configuration evidence does not identify these decidable literal producer conflicts.",
