        {
          "path": "tooling/xtask/test_data/reference_membership/sources/base/bazel/bazel.bzl",
          "line": 1085,
          "fact": "_validate_split_test_filter trims supported leading/trailing forms, splits on dots and rejects non-alphanumeric components."
        },
        {
          "path": "tooling/xtask/test_data/reference_membership/sources/base/bazel/bazel.bzl",
          "line": 1136,
          "fact": "Two missing/falsey filters cause an explicit failure rather than valid aggregate generation."
        }
      ],
      "requested_change": "Retain literal attributes and explicitly classify known producer-rejected filter configurations; suppress trusted split/aggregate membership for them. For filter semantics outside the bounded supported grammar, report unresolved producer constraints instead of accepting them implicitly. Preserve positive filter/manual assertions and add regressions for an invalid string filter and two falsey/missing-filter splits.",
      "acceptance": "Those negative cases retain explicit source rejection/unresolved evidence and no automatic membership/aggregate claim; all 19 existing tests and original fixtures remain intact. Normal locked compilation/test gates still require a runtime lease."
